  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tonga Renewable Energy Stabilisation Package</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Tonga Renewable Energy Stabilisation Package supports the Government of Tonga, through Tonga Power Limited, to increase access and supply of reliable energy and reduce the power sector&apos;s reliance on fossil fuel. The Package has three components (i) upgrading of the main power grid to a 33kV line to enable integration of new solar/battery infrastructure (ii) purchase of three generators that are compatible with new hybrid-grid technology to support Tonga&apos;s renewable energy transition, and their installation and (iii) contribution to the final section of the Nuku&#x2019;alofa Network Upgrade Project (NNUP) to reduce power distribution losses. The Package builds on Australia&apos;s investments in Tonga&apos;s renewable energy transition since 2014 including the Tonga Renewable Energy Project - TREP and Outer Islands Renewable Energy Project - OIREP and earlier phases of NNUP.</narrative>
  </description>
