   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Infrastructure</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Tonga Renewable Energy Stabilisation Package is providing support to Tonga Power Limited (TPL), Tonga&#x2019;s sole energy supplier, to stabilise and upgrade its critical infrastructure. Through the investment, TPL used Australian funds to conduct a comprehensive structural review of the country&#x2019;s major powerhouse in the capital of Nuku&#x2019;alofa which was built in the early 1990s. This was the first comprehensive structural and civil engineering assessment of the powerhouse. It identified an urgent need for structural upgrades including enhanced disaster resilience. The findings directly led to a cabinet decision to prioritise renovating the powerhouse to meet international standards, safeguarding power supply for the next 30 &#x2013; 50 years. Australian funding will contribute to the improved facility. Also a result, TPL has strengthened its approaches to regular reviews and assessments of its infrastructure, in turn improving business continuity and investment planning.</narrative>
    </description>
